    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 4.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.93–0.97 from 6 h onward, which looks like detector saturation. Dilutions of the 18 h aliquot do not scale back to that value. The 10x dilution read 0.478 (replicates 0.481 and 0.475), which is 4.78 when multiplied back. The 25x dilution read 0.182 (4.56 corrected). The 50x dilution read 0.091 (4.57 corrected). The 25x and 50x corrected values agree at about 4.6, which suggests the reader is linear at those readings. The 10x value is slightly higher, so it may also carry some saturation. The true OD at 18 h is therefore about 4.6, roughly 5 times the undiluted reading of 0.92, so the plateau is a reader ceiling rather than the biomass level."
  },
